{"topicSections":[{"title":"Protocols","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PreferenceKey"],"anchor":"Protocols"},{"title":"Storage","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PreferenceValues"],"anchor":"Storage"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Pass data from child views up to their ancestors.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StateManagement","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ThemingGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusSystem","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/AppearanceAndColors","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/CustomViews","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/KeyboardShortcuts","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PaletteReference","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ListAndTable","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/LayoutSystem","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ImageDecoding"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides"}],"metadata":{"title":"Preferences","modules":[{"name":"TUIkit"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TUIkit’s preference system enables "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"bottom-up data flow","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": the reverse of environment values. While the environment passes data down from parent to child, preferences let child views publish values that ancestors can observe and react to."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The system mirrors SwiftUI’s preference API and consists of three parts:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PreferenceKey","isActive":true}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Protocol that defines a named value type with a default and a reduce strategy","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PreferenceValues"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Type-safe storage that holds all preference values for a scope"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"PreferenceStorage","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Stack-based collector that manages preference contexts per render pass","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A built-in example is "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/NavigationTitleKey","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":": a child view sets "},{"code":".navigationTitle(\"Settings\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and the enclosing navigation container reads that preference to render the title bar."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Defining a Preference Key","type":"heading","anchor":"Defining-a-Preference-Key"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A preference key declares what type of value it carries and how multiple values from sibling children are combined:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct CounterKey: PreferenceKey {","    static let defaultValue: Int = 0","","    static func reduce(value: inout Int, nextValue: () -> Int) {","        value += nextValue()","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"defaultValue"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Returned when no child has set this preference"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"reduce(value:nextValue:)","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Combines values when multiple children set the same key"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" implementation simply takes the last value. Override it when you need additive behavior (summing counts), array collection, or other merge strategies."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Setting a Preference","type":"heading","anchor":"Setting-a-Preference"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Child views publish a preference using the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".preference(key:value:)"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct ItemView: View {","    var body: some View {","        Text(\"Item\")","            .preference(key: CounterKey.self, value: 1)","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Under the hood, this wraps the view in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"PreferenceModifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that calls ","type":"text"},{"code":"preferences.setValue(_:forKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" during rendering. The value is reduced into the current scope using the key’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Observing Preferences","type":"heading","anchor":"Observing-Preferences"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ancestor views react to collected preferences using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".onPreferenceChange(_:perform:)"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct ItemList: View {","    var body: some View {","        VStack {","            ItemView()","            ItemView()","            ItemView()","        }","        .onPreferenceChange(CounterKey.self) { totalCount in","            \/\/ totalCount == 3 (three children each set value: 1, additive reduce)","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The modifier pushes a new preference context, renders all children (which set their preferences), pops the context, and fires the callback with the accumulated result."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"The Navigation Title Shortcut","type":"heading","anchor":"The-Navigation-Title-Shortcut"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TUIkit provides "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/NavigationTitleKey"},{"type":"text","text":" as a built-in preference key with a convenience modifier:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct SettingsPage: View {","    var body: some View {","        VStack {","            Text(\"App settings go here\")","        }","        .navigationTitle(\"Settings\")","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"NavigationTitleKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" uses the default ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (last value wins), so the deepest child’s title takes precedence.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"How Preferences Flow per Frame","type":"heading","anchor":"How-Preferences-Flow-per-Frame"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Preferences are collected fresh every frame. Here’s the lifecycle within a single render pass:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reset","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RenderLoop.render()"},{"type":"text","text":" calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preferences.beginRenderPass()"},{"type":"text","text":", clearing all callbacks and resetting the stack to a single empty context"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Set","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": As the view tree renders top-down, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PreferenceModifier"},{"type":"text","text":" views call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setValue(_:forKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which reduces values into the current stack frame"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Scope"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"OnPreferenceChangeModifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pushes a new context before rendering its subtree, isolating child preferences","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Collect","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": After the subtree finishes, the modifier pops the context (merging into the parent) and fires the callback with the scoped result"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Discard"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": At the start of the next frame, everything resets: stale preferences never persist"}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This per-frame reset ensures preferences always reflect the current view tree. Removed views stop contributing automatically."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Reduce Strategies","type":"heading","anchor":"Reduce-Strategies"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":" function determines how multiple children’s values combine. Common patterns:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Strategy","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Implementation"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use Case","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Last value wins"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"value = nextValue()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (default)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Titles, labels: deepest child wins"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Additive","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"value += nextValue()"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Counting items, summing heights","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Array collection"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"value.append(contentsOf: nextValue())"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Gathering menu items, breadcrumbs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"code":["\/\/ Array collection example","struct BreadcrumbKey: PreferenceKey {","    static let defaultValue: [String] = []","","    static func reduce(value: inout [String], nextValue: () -> [String]) {","        value.append(contentsOf: nextValue())","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tuikit\/preferences"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Preferences","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/ThemingGuide":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ThemingGuide","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/themingguide","kind":"article","title":"Theming Guide","abstract":[{"text":"Customize the visual appearance of your TUIkit application with palettes.","type":"text"}]},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/StatusBarGuide":{"kind":"article","role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarGuide","title":"Status Bar","url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/statusbarguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure the shortcut bar at the bottom of the terminal."}]},"doc://TUIkit/documentation